{"availability":"available","full":"erseco/alpine-moodle","name":"alpine-moodle","description":"Moodle docker image based on Alpine Linux","category":"Other","language":"PHP","stars":87,"forks":53,"created":"2020-04-29T17:02:22Z","updated":"2026-10-05T23:26:47Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://erseco.github.io/alpine-moodle/","topics":["alpine","docker","hacktoberfest","lightweight","lms","moodle","nginx","php8"],"demo":"https://erseco.github.io/alpine-moodle/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T20:14:39.911Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T20:14:39.911Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T20:14:39.911Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T20:14:39.911Z","stars":87,"forks":53}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A lightweight Moodle Docker image built on Alpine Linux — PHP 8.4 FPM (8.3 for legacy Moodle tags), Nginx, multi-arch, configured entirely through environment variables.","Since v5.3.0, latest is Moodle 5.3 LTS on PHP 8.4 (it was Moodle 5.2 on PHP 8.3). Moodle 4.5 LTS and 5.0–5.2 tags keep PHP 8.3; pin v4.5.x to stay on the previous LTS. See PHP versions.","The documentation site covers quick start, docker-compose recipes, reverse proxy setups (Traefik, Nginx, NPM, Apache, Caddy), every supported environment variable, persistence and upgrade workflows, and a troubleshooting section built from the most frequent support questions."],"features":["Compact image (100 MB) built on erseco/alpine-php-webserver","PHP 8.4 FPM with ondemand process manager; legacy Moodle tags retain PHP 8.3 (see runtime policy)","PostgreSQL, MariaDB/MySQL or SQLite (single-container dev mode)","Optional Redis session handler","Supports Moodle 4.x, 5.0, 5.1+ (auto-detects /public layout) and main"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/erseco/alpine-moodle/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"83213c031fd98f93374fc653f46d9583bcc7d7a715d0afb0e38c1a5fd2f93dbd","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T20:14:40.002Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-